{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8p4qv1ZYgjPwofs2wJY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013khoEL1yU7Z1RaVNQdF51B","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/nick/code/webtorrent-desktop.memory-leaks-02-engine-forgets-per-torrent-state-on-close; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/engine/AGENTS.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold_start=s.index(\"-- and cleared in `stopTorrenting`.\")\nold_end=s.index(\"The three tunables are exported\")\ns=s[:old_start]+\"\"\"-- and cleared when the torrent closes (see below).\n\n\"\"\" + s[old_end:]\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"## `announce.js`\"\"\",\"\"\"## Per-torrent state and the torrent's `close`\n\nState the engine keys by info hash (`lastAnnounceAt`,\n`corruptPeerStats`, the stall tracker) is forgotten in one place:\n`torrentClose`, the `close` handler `addTorrentEvents` installs.\nWebTorrent emits `close` from `destroy()` whatever the cause --\n`wt-stop-torrenting`, removal, a fatal error -- so `stopTorrenting`\nonly destroys and does not repeat the cleanup. Add new per-torrent\ncleanup to that handler, not to `stopTorrenting`.\n\nThe handler returns early when `client.get(infoHash)` still finds a\ntorrent. WebTorrent removes a closing torrent from the client before\nemitting `close`, so a hit means a duplicate add is being destroyed\nunder the live torrent's hash, and that state is not its to forget.\n\n`test/unit/engine-torrent-close-wiring.js` pins this by source scan.\n\n## `announce.js`\"\"\",1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit diff src/engine/AGENTS.md | head -60"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1118,"cache_read_input_tokens":72167,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1118},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnosti